cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Monte Carlo slip rates: an interactive teaching site"
message: "If you use this teaching material, please cite it. If you use the incremental slip-rate method itself, cite Zinke et al. (2017, 2019) as the RISeR documentation asks."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "La Greca"
    given-names: "James"
    affiliation: "School of Geography, Earth and Atmospheric Sciences, University of Melbourne"
repository-code: "https://github.com/james-lagreca/monte-carlo-slip-rates"
url: "https://james-lagreca.github.io/monte-carlo-slip-rates/"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, dependency-free teaching site on Monte Carlo and incremental
  fault slip-rate estimation. Covers distribution choice, single-marker rate
  distributions, rejection sampling under a monotonicity condition, percentile
  against highest posterior density reporting, onset-of-offset anchoring, and
  the effect of pairing an offset with an age that dates a different event.
  All teaching datasets are synthetic.
keywords:
  - slip rate
  - Monte Carlo
  - incremental slip rate
  - paleoseismology
  - tectonic geomorphology
  - teaching
license: MIT
